---
title: "3 · Pick services and prices"
description: Add packages and services to an opportunity and agree the prices.
sidebar:
  order: 4
  label: "3 · Pick services and prices"
---

**Who:** the person in charge of the opportunity. **Where:** the opportunity › **Services** tab.

{% steps %}

1. Open the opportunity and go to the **Services** tab. The country comes from the opportunity; only the items offered in that country are listed.
2. Search, or filter by category, and select **Add** on a package or a single service. The agreed price starts at the catalog price.
3. Change **Qty** or **Agreed** where needed. The totals and the discount against the catalog (**vs catalog**) are updated as you type.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="crm/services-list" caption="The packages and services offered in the opportunity's country." /%}

## The list of packages and services

The **Add packages and services** list shows the code, category, department, billing and reference price of each item. Filter by department or by category, or search by name or code.

A service marked **Missing contract text** has no wording yet for this country in that language. Generation of a contract in that language stops on it. Ask the department head to add the text under **Services & Packages** (see [2 · Services & Packages](/en/crm/services-packages/)).

{% screenshot id="crm/services-filter-department" caption="Filtering the list by department." /%}

{% aside type="note" title="Prices are changed only here" %}
The **Services** tab is the only place where the services and prices of a deal are changed. Once the opportunity has a contract, the opportunity's amount follows the contract.
{% /aside %}

{% screenshot id="crm/services-added" caption="Two services added at the catalog price." /%}

{% screenshot id="crm/services-agreed-discount" caption="Agreed prices lowered to 20% below the catalog price." /%}

## Example

An opportunity for ABC PTE. LTD. in Singapore needs an annual bookkeeping service and a GST filing service. The person in charge adds both at the catalog price, then lowers the agreed prices by 20% as agreed with the client. The **vs catalog** column shows the discount on each line and on the total.
